            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "<p><strong><strong>Why do we love the way we do and why do some relationships feel so much harder than others?</strong></strong></p><p>Join us as we explore Attached, the bestselling and eye-opening guide to the science of adult relationships. Combining psychology and neuroscience, this book reveals how understanding attachment theory can transform the way we connect, communicate, and build lasting love.</p><p>Based on decades of research, Attached explains that we each tend to develop one of three attachment styles - anxious, avoidant, or secure, and that these patterns shape how we behave in relationships, often without us even realising it.</p><p>In this session, we’ll unpack these attachment styles and explore how they influence everything from attraction to communication and emotional needs.</p><p>You’ll discover how this approach can help you:</p><p>• Understand your own attachment style and relationship patterns<br>• Recognise the styles of partners and others around you<br>• Navigate challenges like anxiety, distance, or miscommunication<br>• Build healthier, more secure, and fulfilling relationships<br>• Make more informed choices in love and connection</p><p>With practical insights, real-life examples, and simple frameworks, Attached offers a powerful roadmap for creating stronger, more meaningful relationships, whether you’re dating, in a partnership, or simply curious about how love works.</p>",
